  "review": {
    "book": "RUT",
    "entityID": "person:naomi_2147",
    "primaryWitnessVersion": "webp-usfx-2026-10-13-35a6adf626e5",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "RUT 1:2",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT01.htm#V2",
        "textualBasisJa": "The name of the man was Elimelech, and the name of his wife Naomi. The names of his two sons were Mahlon and Chilion, Ephrathites of Bethlehem Judah. They came into the country of Moab and lived there."
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 1:3",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT01.htm#V3",
        "textualBasisJa": "Elimelech, Naomi’s husband, died; and she was left with her two sons."
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 1:8",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT01.htm#V8",
        "textualBasisJa": "Naomi said to her two daughters-in-law, “Go, return each of you to her mother’s house. May the LORD deal kindly with you, as you have dealt with the dead and with me."
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 1:11",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT01.htm#V11",
        "textualBasisJa": "Naomi said, “Go back, my daughters. Why do you want to go with me? Do I still have sons in my womb, that they may be your husbands?"
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 1:19",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT01.htm#V19",
        "textualBasisJa": "So they both went until they came to Bethlehem. When they had come to Bethlehem, all the city was excited about them, and they asked, “Is this Naomi?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 1:20",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT01.htm#V20",
        "textualBasisJa": "She said to them, “Don’t call me Naomi. Call me Mara, for the Almighty has dealt very bitterly with me."
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 1:21",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT01.htm#V21",
        "textualBasisJa": "I went out full, and the LORD has brought me home again empty. Why do you call me Naomi, since the LORD has testified against me, and the Almighty has afflicted me?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 1:22",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT01.htm#V22",
        "textualBasisJa": "So Naomi returned, and Ruth the Moabitess, her daughter-in-law, with her, who returned out of the country of Moab. They came to Bethlehem in the beginning of barley harvest."
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 2:1",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT02.htm#V1",
        "textualBasisJa": "Naomi had a relative of her husband’s, a mighty man of wealth, of the family of Elimelech, and his name was Boaz."
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 2:2",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT02.htm#V2",
        "textualBasisJa": "Ruth the Moabitess said to Naomi, “Let me now go to the field, and glean among the ears of grain after him in whose sight I find favor.” She said to her, “Go, my daughter.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 2:6",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT02.htm#V6",
        "textualBasisJa": "The servant who was set over the reapers answered, “It is the Moabite lady who came back with Naomi out of the country of Moab."
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 2:20",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT02.htm#V20",
        "textualBasisJa": "Naomi said to her daughter-in-law, “May he be blessed by the LORD, who has not abandoned his kindness to the living and to the dead.” Naomi said to her, “The man is a close relative to us, one of our near kinsmen.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 2:22",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT02.htm#V22",
        "textualBasisJa": "Naomi said to Ruth her daughter-in-law, “It is good, my daughter, that you go out with his maidens, and that they not harm you in any other field.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 3:1",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT03.htm#V1",
        "textualBasisJa": "Naomi her mother-in-law said to her, “My daughter, shall I not seek rest for you, that it may be well with you?"
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 4:3",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT04.htm#V3",
        "textualBasisJa": "He said to the near kinsman, “Naomi, who has come back out of the country of Moab, is selling the parcel of land, which was our brother Elimelech’s."
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 4:5",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT04.htm#V5",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Boaz said, “On the day you buy the field from the hand of Naomi, you must buy it also from Ruth the Moabitess, the wife of the dead, to raise up the name of the dead on his inheritance.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 4:9",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT04.htm#V9",
        "textualBasisJa": "Boaz said to the elders and to all the people, “You are witnesses today, that I have bought all that was Elimelech’s, and all that was Chilion’s and Mahlon’s, from the hand of Naomi."
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 4:14",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT04.htm#V14",
        "textualBasisJa": "The women said to Naomi, “Blessed be the LORD, who has not left you today without a near kinsman. Let his name be famous in Israel."
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 4:16",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT04.htm#V16",
        "textualBasisJa": "Naomi took the child, laid him in her bosom, and became nurse to him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "RUT 4:17",
        "url": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/RUT04.htm#V17",
        "textualBasisJa": "The women, her neighbors, gave him a name, saying, “A son is born to Naomi”. They named him Obed. He is the father of Jesse, the father of David."
      }
    ],
